id: interface/new-yawn-coordinate-workbench-v0.1
title: "New Yawn coordinate-complete workbench"
kind: interface-contract
status: draft-0.1
version: 0.1.0-draft
updated: 2026-09-01

purpose: >
  Let a person begin with one unconstrained signal while the interface compiles
  a truthful, inspectable, proposal-only View of the existing YAWN orientation
  ontology. The surface makes the emerging coordinate legible without turning
  presentation tiles, model inference, or coverage level into canonical truth,
  authority, identity, or proof.

constitutional_sources:
  orientation: core/orientation.yawn
  orientation_questions: question-packets/orientation-nine.yawn
  orientation_map: schemas/orientation-map.v0.1.schema.json
  inquiry_selection: core/inquiry-selection.yawn
  agency_holarchy: schemas/agency-holarchy.v0.2.schema.json
  objective_holon: schemas/objective-holon.v0.1.schema.json
  new_yawn: interface/new-yawn-v0.1.yawn
  projection_and_aperture: core/projection-and-aperture.yawn
  proof_and_boundary: core/proof-and-boundary.yawn

one_model_rule: >
  This contract does not create a second orientation packet, personal ontology,
  agent ontology, or canonical level system. It projects and edits proposed
  state against orientation-map.v0.1 and the shared nine stable question_key
  values. Every generated answer, placement, objective, agent, relationship,
  or move remains attributed and proposal-only until the corresponding
  principal event or accepted record exists.

surface_budget:
  initial:
    - "one existing free-expression field"
    - "one coordinate identity strip"
    - "one compact ten-cell resolution grid"
    - "Auto-lacuna"
    - "Auto-cohere"
  progressive_disclosure:
    - "one selected cell inspector"
    - "proposal feed with Accept, Correct, Reject, and Inspect source"
    - "full nine-axis map"
    - "candidate parent and lateral relations"
    - "provider/delegate binding details"
  prohibition: >
    The default View may not become a ten-field setup form or ask all nine
    orientation questions at once. Inquiry selection continues to foreground
    at most one highest-leverage question or an explicit hold.

coordinate_header:
  fields:
    image:
      source: "selected identity image or canonical blank sleeping Yawn image"
      canonical: false
    name:
      source: "reported name or explicitly labeled inferred draft label"
      canonical: false
    coordinate:
      source: "unplanted local draft address until Owner Plant"
      canonical: false
    location:
      source: "proposed primary-parent path plus relationship/Arena placement"
      canonical: false
    lifecycle:
      values: [local_draft, proposed, planted, sleeping, orienting, active, holding, retired]
    principal:
      rule: "Name the rightful principal or keep it unknown; never infer authority from a display name."

resolution_grid:
  view_kind: orientation_resolution_projection
  canonical_state: false
  cells:
    - cell_key: identity
      label: Identity
      projects: [scope, perspective, principal, coordinate]
      question: "What is this Yawn, and whose coordinate is it?"
    - cell_key: intelligence
      label: Intelligence
      projects: [provider_binding, delegate_relationship, capability, provenance]
      question: "Which intelligence is currently interpreting or acting here, under what binding?"
      boundary: >
        Provider, model, tool, delegate, Agent, and principal remain distinct.
        Connected means a verified current binding, not a selected logo or
        available model.
    - cell_key: relationship
      label: Relationship
      projects: [placement, perspective, relationship]
      question: "Who or what is in relationship here?"
    - cell_key: arena
      label: Arena
      projects: [placement, current-state, arena, horizon]
      question: "Which relevant field of roles, constraints, and affordances is active?"
    - cell_key: state
      label: Current state
      projects: [current-state]
      question: "What appears to be happening now, and who says so?"
    - cell_key: purpose
      label: Purpose
      projects: [intent, objective_candidate]
      question: "What matters, is needed, protected, learned, or made true—and to whom?"
    - cell_key: lacuna
      label: Lacuna
      projects: [lacuna]
      question: "What decision-relevant absence, dispute, or uncertainty remains?"
    - cell_key: boundary
      label: Boundary
      projects: [boundary, authority]
      question: "What must be protected, and who may decide, disclose, delegate, or act?"
    - cell_key: movement
      label: Movement
      projects: [movement, affordance, candidate_move]
      question: "What inquiry, hold, wait, exit, choice, or bounded move remains possible?"
    - cell_key: proof
      label: Proof
      projects: [proof, consequence, update]
      question: "What would reality have to show for this map or relationship to update?"
  state_vocabulary:
    - missing
    - unknown
    - proposed
    - reported
    - observed
    - accepted
    - disputed
    - stale
    - proof_pending
    - verified
    - not_applicable
  rendering_rule: >
    A cell visualizes attributed coverage and freshness. Brightness, completion,
    order, and size never encode human worth, truth, authority, importance,
    consciousness, or guaranteed capability.

resolution_level:
  name: orientation_resolution_level
  range: [1, 10]
  kind: noncanonical_view_metric
  rule: >
    The level is the highest cumulative guarantee currently represented at the
    coordinate. It may fall when evidence becomes stale, disputed, revoked, or
    structurally incoherent. Proposed content may be shown as proposed coverage
    but cannot satisfy an accepted or verified guarantee.
  rungs:
    1: "The coordinate, principal status, and current intelligence-binding status are explicit—even when the honest value is unknown or unbound."
    2: "The live signal, source boundary, and scope or episode are represented."
    3: "Relationship, proposed placement, Arena, and horizon are represented."
    4: "Perspective, roles, affected parties, and observer stance are represented."
    5: "Attributed current state, resources, constraints, and capabilities are represented."
    6: "Concern, need, value, commitment, and objective candidates are represented without turning desire into authority."
    7: "Decision-relevant lacunae, contradictions, dependencies, and disputes remain visible."
    8: "Safety, privacy, consent, obligation, decision rights, and effect authority are explicit."
    9: "Candidate inquiry/hold/choice/movement and its selection rationale are inspectable; recommendation remains distinct from choice."
    10: "Predicted consequence, verifier, falsifier, proof adjudication, update rule, and replay path are represented."
  boundary:
    - "Level is resolution, not rank, maturity, virtue, intelligence, autonomy, or truth."
    - "Ten of ten does not mean correct."
    - "A simple Yawn may be complete at a lower necessary resolution."
    - "Unknown and not-applicable are valid explicit states; silence is not completion."

input_compilation:
  source_preservation: >
    Preserve the person's exact input as an attributed source event before any
    normalization, extraction, summarization, agent detection, objective
    proposal, or routing proposal.
  first_pass:
    - "resolve or propose principal, scope, and draft coordinate"
    - "map source spans into proposed answers on the nine axes"
    - "type every detection as reported, observed, inferred, assumed, predicted, disputed, or unknown"
    - "surface contradictions and missing hard-gate context"
    - "leave unmapped source spans inspectable"
  forbidden:
    - "silently creating a canonical Agent from a metaphor, emotion, urge, voice, role, or model output"
    - "silently creating or changing primary parentage"
    - "turning salience into relevance, relevance into meaning, or meaning into truth"
    - "turning model confidence into authority"

intelligence_binding:
  definition: >
    A typed, revocable relationship connecting the Yawn coordinate to a
    provider, model, human, service, tool, or delegated Agent for a named
    cognitive or operational capability.
  required_readout:
    - binding_status
    - provider_or_agent_ref
    - role
    - capability_scope
    - authority_scope
    - source_and_version
    - freshness
    - privacy_and_egress
    - cost_boundary
    - revocation_path
  statuses: [unknown, unbound, available, selected, connected_unverified, connected_verified, suspended, revoked]
  invariant: "Intelligence may infer or propose; only a valid grant authorizes an effect."

auto_lacuna:
  action_kind: inquiry_selection_request
  implementation_rule: >
    Reuse core/inquiry-selection.yawn over the current orientation-map revision.
    Do not create a second lacuna-ranking algorithm. Return one selected
    question or explicit hold by default; up to three candidates may appear
    only as an inspectable comparison View.
  output:
    - exact missing or disputed axis
    - selected question_key or hold
    - why this could change orientation or rightful choice
    - source and ranking receipt
    - epistemic status and confidence
    - what answer would update
  authority: "proposal_only"

auto_cohere:
  action_kind: coherence_proposal
  purpose: >
    Compare the local draft with authorized ancestor context, exact-coordinate
    state, relevant lateral relationships, and candidate objectives; propose
    the smallest set of mappings or graph changes that would reduce
    contradiction or duplication without mutating canonical state.
  may_propose:
    - "mapping source spans to existing orientation axes"
    - "correcting an inferred label or objective"
    - "linking to an existing Yawn"
    - "candidate primary parent"
    - "typed lateral relation"
    - "candidate Agent, relationship, Arena, objective, lacuna, or move"
    - "split, merge, or retire review"
  must_show:
    - before and proposed after
    - source refs
    - affected coordinates
    - relation type
    - confidence
    - best alternative
    - unresolved contradiction
    - authority required
    - effect boundary
    - rollback or rejection path
  cannot:
    - "plant a Yawn"
    - "reparent, merge, split, retire, disclose, delegate, execute, or spend"
    - "promote a candidate Agent or objective"
    - "overwrite a reported source"
    - "clear a hard gate"
  acceptance_rule: >
    Accept records the principal's local disposition of the exact proposal.
    It does not establish empirical truth, proof, provider connectivity, or
    effect authority. Canonical graph mutation remains behind Owner Plant or a
    later exact typed grant.

proposal_feed:
  dispositions: [accept_local, correct, reject, defer, inspect]
  record_each:
    - proposal_id
    - source_revision
    - exact_proposed_patch
    - asserted_by
    - epistemic_status
    - confidence
    - principal_disposition
    - disposition_time
    - resulting_local_revision
  preservation_rule: "Rejected and corrected proposals remain replayable; history is not rewritten."

agent_candidate_boundary:
  default: "A detected goal-like process is an agent_candidate, not a canonical Agent."
  promote_when:
    - "it has a distinguishable identity or stable address"
    - "it has a persistent purpose or policy"
    - "it makes discriminating predictions or supports a distinct move"
    - "it has a boundary, memory, capability, or authority that must remain separate"
    - "the rightful principal accepts the representation at the declared resolution"
  merge_or_reject_when: >
    It adds no distinct prediction, boundary, responsibility, or useful
    affordance beyond an existing Agent, role, habit, belief, emotion, or
    relationship model.

holarchy_runtime_rule:
  inherited_context_order:
    - "constitutional invariants and pinned versions"
    - "rightful principal and exact grants"
    - "exact-coordinate accepted state"
    - "nearest accepted ancestor defaults along one acyclic primary-parent chain"
    - "typed relevant lateral relationships by reference"
    - "fresh observations, disputes, lacunae, and proof state"
    - "rebuildable rankings and presentation"
  never_inherit_as_truth:
    - confidence
    - inferred_identity
    - desire
    - target
    - obligation
    - authority
    - privacy_widening
    - agenthood
    - proof
  conflict_rule: >
    Preserve both attributed claims and foreground the conflict. Exact scope may
    narrow an ancestor default; widening privacy or authority requires an exact
    rightful grant.

owner_plant_boundary:
  remains_canonical: true
  rule: >
    Before Plant, the coordinate, mappings, level, relationships, objectives,
    accepted proposals, and provider selections remain an unsaved local View.
    Plant writes an authenticated append-only event containing source,
    dispositions, exact accepted mappings, primary parent, visibility, and
    boundaries. Plant does not authorize later external effects.

illegal_casts:
  - "View -> ontology"
  - "coverage -> truth"
  - "level -> worth or autonomy"
  - "provider -> Agent identity"
  - "available intelligence -> connected intelligence"
  - "salience -> relevance"
  - "relevance -> meaning"
  - "meaning -> truth"
  - "confidence -> authority"
  - "recommendation -> choice"
  - "choice -> authorization"
  - "capability -> permission"
  - "acceptance -> proof"
  - "move -> consequence"
  - "consequence -> proof"
  - "child grant -> parent authority"

proof:
  current_status: contract_proposed
  smallest_product_test: >
    Given one free-expression signal, the New Yawn View preserves the exact
    source; shows a draft coordinate and ten-cell resolution projection; maps
    only attributed proposals to the existing nine-axis Orientation Map;
    returns proposal-only Auto-lacuna and Auto-cohere candidates; records local
    Accept/Correct/Reject dispositions; and creates no persistence, graph
    mutation, provider connection, authority grant, or external effect before
    Owner Plant.
  falsifiers:
    - "The surface requires the person to complete a setup form before expression."
    - "A model-generated field appears as reported or accepted without attribution."
    - "Auto-cohere changes parentage or identity without an exact principal event."
    - "Level is interpreted as intelligence, worth, truth, or permission."
    - "A provider appears connected without a verified binding."
    - "The implementation creates a parallel orientation object instead of orientation-map.v0.1."

links:
  - interface/new-yawn-v0.1.yawn
  - core/orientation.yawn
  - core/inquiry-selection.yawn
  - question-packets/orientation-nine.yawn
  - schemas/orientation-map.v0.1.schema.json
  - schemas/agency-holarchy.v0.2.schema.json
  - schemas/objective-holon.v0.1.schema.json
